A 2020 arXiv research paper by Kevin Rao. \mathbf{Abstract}

Machine learning algorithms are designed to make accurate predictions of the future based on existing data, while online algorithms seek to bound some performance measure (typically the competitive ratio) without knowledge of the future. Lykouris and Vassilvitskii
[
3
]
demonstrated that augmenting online algorithms with a machine learned predictor can provably decrease the competitive ratio under as long as the predictor is suitably accurate.
